<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>InfoTop: Program to extract information from Top-MiraMon vector
  files</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
   <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

  <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 

  <ul>
    <li>The first page of information shows a list of the files linked to the
    requested file. If any of them is lacking, the program notifies it; if the
    lacking file is not essential for the program operation, it is allowed to
    continue.</li>

    <li>The second page gives information on the files' header. They show
    the number of entities (graphic objects) and the global bounding rectangles
    of the files.<br/></li>

    <li>The third page is a menu that allows:

      <p>In the case of <u>arc or polygon</u> files:</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>1 Visualization of an arc.</dt>

        <dd>You can see all the information contained in the ARC file but the
        vertices. You can also see the coordinates of the initial and final
        nodes. If you have selected a polygon file the right and left polygon
        indices of the arc are shown.</dd>

        <dt>2 Visualization of a node.</dt>

        <dd>You can see the number of arcs that converge to a node.</dd>

        <dt>3 Visualization of the vertices of an arc.</dt>

        <dd>You can see the coordinates of all the vertices of an arc.</dd>

        <dt>4 Visualization of polygons (only if a polygon file has been
        indicated)</dt>

        <dd>You can see the general information of each polygon contained in
        the POL file, as well as the arc identifiers of the polygon. For each
        arc it is shown whether the arc belongs to the interior or the
        exterior border of the polygon, if it is a final arc of an elemental
        polygon (ring) and if, in order to build the polygon, it is required
        to list the arc coordinates in the original order or in reversed
        order.</dd>
      </dl>

      <p>In the case of <u>point</u> files:</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>1 Visualization of the point coordinates from a given point
        on.</dt>
      </dl>

      <p>In <u>all cases</u> you can also view the database. There are two
      options:</p>

      <dl>
        <dt>1 Visualization of the database fields.</dt>

        <dd>A list of the field names of the main (principal) and associated
        tables is shown, along with their relationships, and if they are
        declared visible or not in the REL file.</dd>

        <dt>2 Visualization of database records.</dt>

        <dd>(For more details see the help of LECTDBF)</dd>
      </dl>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
 <!-- Aquí inicia la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpssintaxi"/>
<!-- Aquí acaba la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon editable de el WPS.-->
<p><!-- $$EXCLUSIVA$$
To obtain the complete help, please type:
INFOTOP ?
--></p>

  </exclusiva>
This program works with files of v. 1.1<br/>

